1
00:00:14,745 --> 00:00:17,145
(Eight Seconds Ago)

2
00:00:17,205 --> 00:00:20,607
Rin, your positioning was very precise.

3
00:00:20,667 --> 00:00:22,659
Based on Bachira's previous habits,

4
00:00:22,719 --> 00:00:25,069
he would definitely pass the ball
at a certain moment.

5
00:00:25,129 --> 00:00:26,959
The direction you headed was

6
00:00:27,019 --> 00:00:29,532
the best position to receive the pass.

7
00:00:29,592 --> 00:00:32,345
However, he's different now.

8
00:00:32,845 --> 00:00:34,597
I will devour him.

9
00:00:35,473 --> 00:00:38,310
Right now, no one can see
the direction of Bachira's kick.

10
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:41,479
Only someone who can see everything
and keep breaking through the future.

11
00:00:42,095 --> 00:00:45,155
I've always received Bachira's passes,
so I can see it.

12
00:00:45,216 --> 00:00:48,111
The old Bachira
wouldn't have chosen a selfish move.

13
00:00:48,609 --> 00:00:50,261
In the end,

14
00:00:50,321 --> 00:00:53,616
the one who still believed in you—
I'm the winner.

15
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:56,226
Isagi.

16
00:00:56,286 --> 00:00:58,850
Bachira, I always believed in you.

17
00:00:58,910 --> 00:01:01,666
You could break through here on your own.

18
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:04,566
At this moment,

19
00:01:04,626 --> 00:01:08,798
Yoichi Isagi's level has undoubtedly
surpassed Rin Itoshi.

20
00:01:10,258 --> 00:01:12,859
If the angle of Yoichi Isagi's right foot

21
00:01:12,919 --> 00:01:14,890
that stopped Meguru Bachira's shot

22
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:17,060
had deviated by just one more centimeter,

23
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:21,032
the fate of this eight-person match
might have been different.

24
00:01:21,093 --> 00:01:25,672
But the ball fell randomly,
unfeelingly,

25
00:01:25,732 --> 00:01:28,270
and cruelly

26
00:01:28,330 --> 00:01:32,155
in front of the winner.

27
00:01:45,177 --> 00:01:47,694
The match is over.

28
00:01:47,754 --> 00:01:49,696
Score, 5-4.

29
00:01:49,756 --> 00:01:52,216
The red team wins.

30
00:01:55,136 --> 00:01:57,330
Great!

31
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:03,019
I can now fight on my own.

32
00:02:03,845 --> 00:02:07,297
Heading towards my soccer belief
that needs no one else.

33
00:02:07,357 --> 00:02:11,008
- Into a world where I'm alone,
- Why? Damn it!

34
00:02:11,068 --> 00:02:14,410
- I finally stepped into it.
- Why?

35
00:02:15,790 --> 00:02:17,040
Isagi.

36
00:02:17,867 --> 00:02:19,660
Well done.

37
00:02:20,619 --> 00:02:22,945
Let me savor this feeling of victory.

38
00:02:23,006 --> 00:02:24,060
Sorry.

39
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,730
So, who are we going to take?

40
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:29,068
About this... are we two choosing again?

41
00:02:29,128 --> 00:02:31,590
Wait a moment.

42
00:02:31,650 --> 00:02:34,520
Even without Isagi,
I could have survived too.

43
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:37,160
So, I'll say it proudly.

44
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:38,810
I...

45
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:40,955
The person I want to choose...

46
00:02:41,015 --> 00:02:43,393
Shut up! I'm the one choosing.

47
00:02:44,830 --> 00:02:45,585
Rin?

48
00:02:45,645 --> 00:02:48,296
No objections.

49
00:02:48,356 --> 00:02:50,390
That last ball,

50
00:02:50,450 --> 00:02:52,759
I completely didn't expect it.

51
00:02:52,819 --> 00:02:55,600
This is the first time

52
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,824
I've felt failure here.

53
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:01,980
One more person has been added
to those I want to crush.

54
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:02,912
Damn it.

55
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,689
I'm not going to stay quiet.

56
00:03:06,749 --> 00:03:09,776
Come here, Yoichi Isagi!

57
00:03:09,836 --> 00:03:12,779
Be in the closest place to me

58
00:03:12,839 --> 00:03:15,790
to watch me become number one in the world.

59
00:03:19,345 --> 00:03:21,229
(Rin Itoshi, Jyubei Aryu, Aoshi Tokimitsu)

60
00:03:21,289 --> 00:03:22,690
(Meguru Bachira, and Yoichi Isagi)

61
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:26,978
(These Five Advance)

62
00:03:28,290 --> 00:03:31,983
(Episode 23: Luck)

63
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:36,362
Why did you choose me?

64
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:42,975
I couldn't beat him.

65
00:03:43,035 --> 00:03:44,936
What should I do?

66
00:03:44,996 --> 00:03:47,146
What is it that I lack, really?

67
00:03:47,206 --> 00:03:52,420
No one knew where that ball would fall.

68
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:57,383
Between me and Rin,
is the only difference luck?

69
00:03:58,843 --> 00:04:00,770
Come on, Isagi!

70
00:04:00,830 --> 00:04:02,597
Huh? Oh...

71
00:04:04,056 --> 00:04:07,770
I can't, my mind is a mess.

72
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,770
I clearly lost, but he chose me instead.

73
00:04:11,022 --> 00:04:13,483
Guys, sorry.

74
00:04:17,361 --> 00:04:21,600
We almost won and made it into the top three.

75
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:23,730
That last goal was entirely luck.

76
00:04:23,790 --> 00:04:24,767
We didn't really lose...

77
00:04:24,827 --> 00:04:26,787
I don't need your consolation.

78
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:30,810
Rin chose you,

79
00:04:30,870 --> 00:04:32,400
that's a fact.

80
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:34,861
Shut up and keep moving forward.

81
00:04:34,921 --> 00:04:37,196
Right.

82
00:04:37,256 --> 00:04:39,639
If I see that face of yours again,

83
00:04:39,699 --> 00:04:41,730
I'll definitely kill you.

84
00:04:41,790 --> 00:04:43,828
Get lost, Loser!

85
00:04:43,888 --> 00:04:45,640
Right.

86
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:48,890
You were the protagonist of this team.

87
00:04:48,950 --> 00:04:52,355
A result like this is only natural
for us supporting characters.

88
00:04:53,330 --> 00:04:56,100
When we meet again,
I'll defeat you.

89
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:58,980
Even without you, I can still advance.

90
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:01,390
If it weren't for them,

91
00:05:01,451 --> 00:05:03,723
I wouldn't have been able to
keep striving until now.

92
00:05:03,783 --> 00:05:06,559
This whole time,
was really full of energy.

93
00:05:06,619 --> 00:05:07,685
Nagi.

94
00:05:07,745 --> 00:05:08,811
Barou.

95
00:05:08,871 --> 00:05:09,979
Chigiri.

96
00:05:10,039 --> 00:05:12,648
Being able to fight alongside you

97
00:05:12,708 --> 00:05:15,216
was an honor for me.

98
00:05:15,276 --> 00:05:16,921
You guys have to catch up.

99
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:20,383
Let's play against each other again someday.

100
00:05:29,433 --> 00:05:31,709
Damn it.

101
00:05:31,769 --> 00:05:34,921
Don't think it'll end just like that.

102
00:05:34,981 --> 00:05:38,132
Right, we have to get revenge.

103
00:05:38,192 --> 00:05:42,405
(Nagi, Barou, Chigiri,
Demoted to the Third Stage)

104
00:05:44,865 --> 00:05:47,391
Please guide me, Isagi.

105
00:05:47,451 --> 00:05:51,060
Making Rin choose you,
you're really amazing.

106
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:54,100
Actually, I also planned to choose you.

107
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,451
Thank you.

108
00:05:55,511 --> 00:05:56,859
To be honest,

109
00:05:56,919 --> 00:06:00,361
I'd rather have chosen
the stylish Chigiri.

110
00:06:00,421 --> 00:06:04,152
But your back heel shot
was also very cool.

111
00:06:04,212 --> 00:06:06,577
Welcome, Yoichi Isagi.

112
00:06:06,637 --> 00:06:08,560
Thanks for the compliment.

113
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:10,440
No need to be so formal.

114
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,166
Welcome to the top three.

115
00:06:12,226 --> 00:06:15,270
I accidentally acted like a senior.

116
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:16,810
Don't feel like I'm
abusing power to harass you.

117
00:06:16,870 --> 00:06:17,850
This atmosphere is so bad.

118
00:06:17,910 --> 00:06:20,568
Let me refresh the mood.

119
00:06:21,450 --> 00:06:25,270
Isagi, before you said you would take me,

120
00:06:25,330 --> 00:06:26,556
now it's reversed.

121
00:06:26,616 --> 00:06:29,350
Yes, I'm sorry.

122
00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:30,919
I'm very embarrassed.

123
00:06:30,979 --> 00:06:32,186
No problem,

124
00:06:32,246 --> 00:06:36,580
I can now play even without you.

125
00:06:37,793 --> 00:06:41,980
In the past, I was very afraid
of playing alone.

126
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:44,520
I thought you were my savior.

127
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:47,261
But after this match,
I understand

128
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:51,223
only I can save myself.

129
00:06:52,767 --> 00:06:54,458
I'll keep charging forward
with this thought,

130
00:06:54,518 --> 00:06:56,440
and you're ahead of me.

131
00:06:56,500 --> 00:07:00,715
We really surpassed Rin at that moment.

132
00:07:00,775 --> 00:07:03,310
Thank you, Isagi.

133
00:07:03,370 --> 00:07:06,100
The current me can now
fight alone even without you.

134
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:08,616
It's just that everything
is more interesting when you're around.

135
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:15,020
But if you can't keep up with me,

136
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:17,324
I'll discard you anytime.

137
00:07:17,384 --> 00:07:19,233
What the hell? So arrogant.

138
00:07:19,293 --> 00:07:21,736
Anyway, please take care of me from now on.

139
00:07:21,796 --> 00:07:25,689
Bachira... has really matured.

140
00:07:26,135 --> 00:07:26,884
Okay.

141
00:07:28,094 --> 00:07:29,512
Try getting hit.

142
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:31,996
Faked me out.

143
00:07:32,056 --> 00:07:33,600
Damn it,

144
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:36,160
this part of you never changes.

145
00:07:38,521 --> 00:07:40,129
Rin.

146
00:07:40,189 --> 00:07:41,890
Tell me,

147
00:07:41,950 --> 00:07:43,651
why did I lose to you?

148
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:48,790
What do I lack to be able to beat you?

149
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:52,810
Even an idiot knows,

150
00:07:52,870 --> 00:07:53,601
you lack "luck".

151
00:07:53,661 --> 00:07:55,230
Don't go,

152
00:07:55,290 --> 00:07:57,730
I can't accept lacking an uncertain aspect like luck!

153
00:07:57,790 --> 00:07:59,140
To become stronger,

154
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:01,001
give me a reason I can accept!

155
00:08:02,712 --> 00:08:06,390
The aspect of "luck"
doesn't happen by chance,

156
00:08:06,450 --> 00:08:09,190
but comes to the person who
fights for their hope.

157
00:08:09,250 --> 00:08:10,618
It's a certainty on the field.

158
00:08:10,678 --> 00:08:13,560
If you don't even understand that,

159
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:16,392
you don't deserve to be in the world of winners.

160
00:08:18,450 --> 00:08:20,920
Hey there, unpolished talents.

161
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:24,006
Congratulations on passing
the second selection.

162
00:08:24,066 --> 00:08:26,890
The meaning of luck

163
00:08:26,950 --> 00:08:28,969
is indeed a very interesting topic.

164
00:08:29,029 --> 00:08:32,230
Alright, step over to the next side.

165
00:08:32,289 --> 00:08:35,350
To celebrate your success,
I will tell you

166
00:08:35,409 --> 00:08:39,522
what kind of figure luck is
in the world of soccer.

167
00:08:39,582 --> 00:08:41,390
Luck is luck,

168
00:08:41,450 --> 00:08:43,669
there's no other possibility
besides coincidence.

169
00:08:45,290 --> 00:08:49,140
Ordinary people who fail can only
rely on that weightless brain,

170
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,783
then use these words
to twist reality.

171
00:08:50,843 --> 00:08:52,910
Listen to me calmly.

172
00:08:53,830 --> 00:08:55,871
I'll ask you a question.

173
00:08:55,931 --> 00:08:59,310
Have you ever been hit by bird droppings?

174
00:09:00,435 --> 00:09:02,545
Isn't that very bad?

175
00:09:02,605 --> 00:09:06,006
After being hit by bird droppings,

176
00:09:06,066 --> 00:09:08,509
you realize there are many
bird droppings around.

177
00:09:08,569 --> 00:09:11,846
When you look up,
there are many birds above.

178
00:09:11,906 --> 00:09:15,520
If you could have realized earlier
and avoided it,

179
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:18,769
could you call it "bad luck"?

180
00:09:18,829 --> 00:09:21,060
This... what is he talking about?

181
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:23,890
We were talking about luck,
why is he talking about bird droppings?

182
00:09:23,950 --> 00:09:25,151
I'll ask another question.

183
00:09:25,211 --> 00:09:27,890
- For example, a summer festival lottery.
- Too bad, you're unlucky.

184
00:09:27,950 --> 00:09:31,310
If the shop owner
didn't put in a "winner",

185
00:09:31,370 --> 00:09:34,493
can the person who got
"you're unlucky" be called "unlucky"?

186
00:09:34,553 --> 00:09:36,690
What are you really talking about?

187
00:09:36,750 --> 00:09:39,457
Luck isn't always there,

188
00:09:39,517 --> 00:09:42,825
but it will come to the place
it has to visit.

189
00:09:42,885 --> 00:09:45,390
It's the same on the field.

190
00:09:45,450 --> 00:09:47,423
Think about it in a 90-minute
soccer match,

191
00:09:47,483 --> 00:09:50,716
"coincidence" and "certainty"
happen continuously.

192
00:09:51,236 --> 00:09:52,720
If you think about it,

193
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:55,222
the chance of appearing again
from zero to one

194
00:09:55,282 --> 00:09:57,975
has a shooting formula
from one's own skill.

195
00:09:58,035 --> 00:10:01,390
Everything you learned at Blue Lock

196
00:10:01,450 --> 00:10:04,815
could be called training
to increase the "certainty" of shooting.

197
00:10:04,875 --> 00:10:06,230
And then,

198
00:10:06,290 --> 00:10:09,445
when we and the opponent
definitely collide,

199
00:10:09,505 --> 00:10:12,060
a "coincidence" no one can predict
will emerge.

200
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:14,533
This is the epicenter of "luck".

201
00:10:14,593 --> 00:10:16,827
Likewise with the last ball,

202
00:10:16,887 --> 00:10:19,270
player 16 slipped past the marking
by dribbling,

203
00:10:19,330 --> 00:10:21,599
then when about to shoot,

204
00:10:21,659 --> 00:10:24,627
those who slowed down
and stopped were these five people.

205
00:10:24,687 --> 00:10:27,890
Except player 15 kept running knowing
that player 16 would pass the marking,

206
00:10:27,950 --> 00:10:31,270
the other five thought they had to stop
and check the shooting conditions.

207
00:10:31,330 --> 00:10:33,093
At this time, only one person.

208
00:10:33,153 --> 00:10:35,599
Player 1 not only didn't stop,

209
00:10:35,659 --> 00:10:37,556
but immediately ran fast
towards player 15.

210
00:10:37,616 --> 00:10:40,440
Player 1 assessed that player 16
wouldn't pass to him

211
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,478
and directly caught
the movement of player 15,

212
00:10:42,538 --> 00:10:47,566
charging forward by betting
"the goal will bounce".

213
00:10:47,626 --> 00:10:49,600
Wait a moment.

214
00:10:49,660 --> 00:10:51,230
Maybe what you say is true,

215
00:10:51,290 --> 00:10:53,730
but the ball falling in front of him
surely isn't a coincidence, right?

216
00:10:53,790 --> 00:10:56,158
The ball could have bounced to anyone's side.

217
00:10:56,218 --> 00:10:57,640
Yes,

218
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:01,307
but you mean this could
become "my ball", right?

219
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:07,480
Suppose player 1
also slowed down at that time,

220
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:10,520
the ball might have bounced in front of him.

221
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:13,270
Even if the person in that position
got the ball,

222
00:11:13,330 --> 00:11:17,346
the opponent's defender would also pounce
before the shot was made.

223
00:11:17,406 --> 00:11:18,390
In other words,

224
00:11:18,450 --> 00:11:20,429
for a striker,

225
00:11:20,489 --> 00:11:21,976
this is the "you're unlucky" position.

226
00:11:22,036 --> 00:11:24,478
So, player 1 increased speed

227
00:11:24,538 --> 00:11:27,270
and ran to the position
most likely to score a goal.

228
00:11:27,330 --> 00:11:29,440
Only one person ran
to that possible "success" spot

229
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:31,211
and waited for "luck" to arrive.

230
00:11:32,922 --> 00:11:34,440
I see.

231
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:36,310
Rin ran to the spot most likely
to get hit by bird droppings

232
00:11:36,370 --> 00:11:38,850
and created a chance
for a goal recurrence.

233
00:11:38,910 --> 00:11:40,035
That sounds very disgusting.

234
00:11:40,095 --> 00:11:44,748
Of course, that ball could also
fall to the opposing team.

235
00:11:44,808 --> 00:11:50,390
At that time, it might counterattack
and change the outcome of the match.

236
00:11:50,450 --> 00:11:55,000
Matches are that tense
and incredibly exciting.

237
00:11:57,580 --> 00:12:01,310
Even though in the end he won
because of "luck",

238
00:12:01,370 --> 00:12:03,849
others could only
stand by

239
00:12:03,909 --> 00:12:07,450
and missed the chance
for "luck" to arrive.

240
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:09,899
That's very normal.

241
00:12:09,959 --> 00:12:13,890
They haven't mentally prepared
to accept "coincidence".

242
00:12:13,950 --> 00:12:17,114
It's too late to think
after "luck" arrives.

243
00:12:17,174 --> 00:12:20,075
You have to improve your ability

244
00:12:20,135 --> 00:12:25,520
until you can stand in any position
to seize that chance.

245
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:28,644
The goddess of luck will only smile

246
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:32,254
upon those who have
a strong sense of intuition.

247
00:12:32,314 --> 00:12:35,382
In a soccer match,
there is indeed "luck" and "chance".

248
00:12:35,442 --> 00:12:40,197
Do you still consider this match result
a coincidence?

249
00:12:41,450 --> 00:12:44,350
People who are toyed with by fate are
players still in the middle class.

250
00:12:44,410 --> 00:12:46,894
If this is the result of hard work,
then puff out your chest.

251
00:12:46,954 --> 00:12:51,815
Be the person who stands in front
and regrets the "coincidence" result.

252
00:12:51,875 --> 00:12:57,370
Fate will only fairly arrive
on the side of those who fight.

253
00:12:58,215 --> 00:13:01,080
Is that what "luck" means?

254
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:04,805
Rin, you're really this amazing.

255
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:06,850
This is nothing.

256
00:13:06,910 --> 00:13:09,583
But, what that Annoying Glasses said
isn't entirely true.

257
00:13:09,643 --> 00:13:14,950
To me, even if that ball wasn't a goal,
there was still another path to take.

258
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:19,403
That wasn't a situation
that appeared under my control.

259
00:13:20,540 --> 00:13:26,243
Just that, the "chance" you created
fell right in front of me.

260
00:13:28,750 --> 00:13:32,270
I only beat you
with "luck".

261
00:13:32,330 --> 00:13:36,100
That goal made me accept this fact,

262
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:39,000
reminding me of the chains of the fact
that I had once lost to you.

263
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,323
The distance between me and Rin

264
00:13:41,383 --> 00:13:43,060
is just

265
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:46,221
determination and whether or not
to accept the fate of a match result.

266
00:13:47,330 --> 00:13:49,940
I'm truly pathetic.

267
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:53,419
I thought I had reached
Rin's ability level, no...

268
00:13:53,479 --> 00:13:56,000
I even felt I had surpassed him.

269
00:13:57,330 --> 00:14:00,384
But actually, I had lost.

270
00:14:00,444 --> 00:14:03,100
I was chosen after losing.

271
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:05,440
I have to accept this fact.

272
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:07,099
There's no next time.

273
00:14:07,159 --> 00:14:10,352
I'll insert the puzzle piece
of "luck" into my thinking

274
00:14:10,412 --> 00:14:13,648
and update the knowledge in my brain.

275
00:14:13,708 --> 00:14:15,190
To defeat Rin,

276
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:19,213
I need a new me!

277
00:14:19,421 --> 00:14:23,866
Alright, your second selection
has ended.

278
00:14:23,926 --> 00:14:28,454
In this selection, you must
have learned how to trigger a chemical reaction.

279
00:14:28,514 --> 00:14:31,327
Next is the third selection.

280
00:14:31,388 --> 00:14:32,777
As previously mentioned,

281
00:14:32,837 --> 00:14:35,681
a strengthening training camp
with the world's best soccer players will be held.

282
00:14:35,741 --> 00:14:38,885
(Third Selection)
After 24 hours,

283
00:14:38,945 --> 00:14:42,361
you will play a five-on-five match
against the best players from various countries.

284
00:14:42,989 --> 00:14:45,304
Frogs in a well
who have been in this cage,

285
00:14:45,364 --> 00:14:48,200
it's time to see the outside world.

286
00:14:50,035 --> 00:14:51,995
(Blue Lock)

287
00:14:53,664 --> 00:14:54,998
(Blue Lock)

288
00:14:56,211 --> 00:14:56,938
So...

289
00:14:57,835 --> 00:14:58,850
(Real Madrid Noble,
Spanish National Team Representative, Leonardo Luna)

290
00:14:58,910 --> 00:15:00,600
Luna, the noble of Real Madrid,

291
00:15:00,660 --> 00:15:02,422
from Spain's famous soccer club.

292
00:15:02,798 --> 00:15:04,600
(Shooting Addict,
England National Team Representative, Adam Blake)

293
00:15:04,660 --> 00:15:07,302
Adam Blake, the top scorer
in the English tournament.

294
00:15:07,594 --> 00:15:08,890
(Freckled Kid,
Argentina National Team Representative, Pablo Cavasoz)

295
00:15:08,950 --> 00:15:10,770
The world's number one free kicker,

296
00:15:10,830 --> 00:15:12,410
Freckled Kid, Cavasoz.

297
00:15:12,933 --> 00:15:13,954
(Heavy Tank,
Brazil National Team Representative, Dada Silva)

298
00:15:14,015 --> 00:15:17,628
Dada Silva, the Heavy Tank born
in the slums, hungry for victory.

299
00:15:17,688 --> 00:15:19,440
Crap.

300
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:21,850
All of them are indeed the best strikers
from around the world.

301
00:15:21,910 --> 00:15:25,792
Tokimitsu, are you a soccer journalist?

302
00:15:25,852 --> 00:15:26,822
If you have questions, just ask me.

303
00:15:27,790 --> 00:15:29,980
What an amazing lineup.

304
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:31,433
Do we have to play

305
00:15:31,493 --> 00:15:34,144
against these players?

306
00:15:34,204 --> 00:15:38,410
Are you guys feeling excited and fired up?

307
00:15:39,209 --> 00:15:42,578
But, I don't seem to know the person
with the crew cut in the middle.

308
00:15:42,638 --> 00:15:43,422
That's true.

309
00:15:44,466 --> 00:15:45,170
(Prodigy,
France National Team Representative, Julian Loki)

310
00:15:45,230 --> 00:15:47,100
His name is Julian Loki,

311
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:50,770
a rising star player who's been showing
his skills in the French tournament lately.

312
00:15:50,830 --> 00:15:52,329
A little info, he's 17 years old this year.

313
00:15:52,389 --> 00:15:54,060
17 years old?

314
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,390
Almost the same age as me,
but already a French national team player.

315
00:15:56,450 --> 00:15:57,709
As long as we beat him,

316
00:15:57,769 --> 00:16:02,149
we'll be recognized
by the whole world, right?

317
00:16:04,910 --> 00:16:06,450
Oh, yeah. Where's Rin?

318
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:10,370
Every day, Rin goes off
alone at the end of the day.

319
00:16:14,453 --> 00:16:16,413
(Training Room)

320
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:24,736
What are you doing?

321
00:16:24,796 --> 00:16:27,520
I want to catch up to you,
so I'm imitating you.

322
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,259
This movement is actually quite painful.

323
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:31,118
Idiot.

324
00:16:31,178 --> 00:16:33,480
Why are you doing this?

325
00:16:33,540 --> 00:16:35,406
This is a gymnastics exercise.

326
00:16:35,466 --> 00:16:37,457
Yoga and meditation to relax the body.

327
00:16:37,517 --> 00:16:40,043
Amazing. Do you have to do it every day?

328
00:16:40,103 --> 00:16:42,615
What about it?

329
00:16:42,675 --> 00:16:44,233
Don't disturb me, or get out.

330
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:51,263
Defeating Sae Itoshi is
the entirety of my soccer.

331
00:16:51,323 --> 00:16:54,520
I've always wanted to ask before.

332
00:16:54,580 --> 00:16:57,204
Is your relationship with your older brother
really bad?

333
00:16:58,540 --> 00:17:00,666
It seems like it.

334
00:17:05,790 --> 00:17:06,849
Not bad.

335
00:17:06,910 --> 00:17:11,742
As long as I win, then the conflict
between us can be resolved.

336
00:17:11,801 --> 00:17:14,559
So serious.

337
00:17:14,618 --> 00:17:17,873
I really have to devour you
to become stronger.

338
00:17:17,933 --> 00:17:21,144
Rin, you're my rival.

339
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:26,632
To me, you're nobody.

340
00:17:26,692 --> 00:17:28,020
What?

341
00:17:28,079 --> 00:17:30,940
As I recall, Rin is a year younger
than me, right?

342
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,221
Arrogant brat.

343
00:17:32,281 --> 00:17:35,730
That match, that moment,

344
00:17:35,790 --> 00:17:38,127
I did lose to you.

345
00:17:38,187 --> 00:17:40,771
But, that moment will
never happen again.

346
00:17:40,831 --> 00:17:43,730
What kind of relaxing exercise is this?

347
00:17:43,790 --> 00:17:46,151
There's no yoga style like this, is there?

348
00:17:46,211 --> 00:17:49,488
This is my lifelong style
that you'll never be able to beat.

349
00:17:49,548 --> 00:17:51,270
Damn.

350
00:17:51,330 --> 00:17:53,060
Even though I can't catch up now,

351
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:55,452
I will definitely
beat him one day!

352
00:17:55,512 --> 00:17:57,222
Don't underestimate me!

353
00:18:02,450 --> 00:18:05,480
Sorry, I got carried away.

354
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:13,136
I got eliminated in the prefectural tournament,

355
00:18:13,196 --> 00:18:16,660
but instead I get to play
against world-class players.

356
00:18:21,872 --> 00:18:24,520
Now is not the time
to be grateful for the situation!

357
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:26,335
I have to become even stronger!

358
00:18:27,410 --> 00:18:28,587
Isagi!

359
00:18:29,290 --> 00:18:30,390
Are you training?

360
00:18:30,450 --> 00:18:31,363
I'll train with you.

361
00:18:31,423 --> 00:18:33,060
Bachira?

362
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:35,615
But, we have to play tomorrow morning.

363
00:18:35,675 --> 00:18:37,560
Aren't you also training?

364
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:39,250
That's true.

365
00:18:41,268 --> 00:18:42,562
Inside my body,

366
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:45,043
there's no longer a monster.

367
00:18:45,103 --> 00:18:49,649
I remember you once said you could hear
a monster's voice when playing soccer.

368
00:18:50,830 --> 00:18:54,803
But now, I play soccer
by listening to my own voice.

369
00:18:54,863 --> 00:18:59,300
For me, this is the meaning
of coming to Blue Lock

370
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:01,578
and meeting you.

371
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,856
He's still a weird person
whose thoughts are hard to understand.

372
00:19:05,916 --> 00:19:08,191
But, he always...

373
00:19:08,251 --> 00:19:10,462
gives me courage!

374
00:19:14,383 --> 00:19:16,700
Let's conquer the world-class selection match!

375
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:17,850
Not bad!

376
00:19:17,910 --> 00:19:19,763
Stay this egotistical!

377
00:19:51,545 --> 00:19:54,297
(Third Selection, Match Field)

378
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:59,618
Much weaker than I thought!

379
00:19:59,678 --> 00:20:02,919
Look at these Japanese,
they're not muscular at all!

380
00:20:02,979 --> 00:20:06,083
I won the bet,
give me 10,000 yen.

381
00:20:06,143 --> 00:20:08,140
Looks like they're laughing at us.

382
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:11,100
They're speaking English.
I don't understand.

383
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:11,963
Me neither.

384
00:20:12,023 --> 00:20:15,620
They're looking down on us.

385
00:20:16,450 --> 00:20:18,230
Aryu, you can speak English?

386
00:20:18,290 --> 00:20:20,140
No, I can only understand it.

387
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,890
I like listening to Western music.

388
00:20:21,950 --> 00:20:24,390
You must spend it on women, right?

389
00:20:24,450 --> 00:20:27,690
Shut up. You came to Japan
for part-time work too.

390
00:20:27,750 --> 00:20:29,480
I want to visit Harajuku.

391
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:31,940
Hey, what do you mean?

392
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,129
For you, is this match
just a part-time job?

393
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:35,850
Rin?

394
00:20:35,910 --> 00:20:37,989
Rin can speak English? Cool!

395
00:20:38,049 --> 00:20:38,840
(Brazil National Team Representative,
Heavy Tank, Dada Silva)

396
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:44,204
Yeah, no one would come here
if it weren't for the extra income.

397
00:20:44,264 --> 00:20:46,600
Listen well.
I'm going to crush you all.

398
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:50,544
Your sightseeing trip to Japan
will become a lifelong trauma.

399
00:20:50,604 --> 00:20:53,064
You've got a big mouth, Damn Brat.

400
00:20:53,773 --> 00:20:55,560
Alright, that's enough.

401
00:20:55,620 --> 00:20:57,690
You three are very childish.

402
00:20:57,750 --> 00:20:59,350
You're Rin Itoshi, right?

403
00:20:59,410 --> 00:21:01,680
I've heard about you from Ego.

404
00:21:01,740 --> 00:21:03,190
You're Sae Itoshi's younger brother.

405
00:21:03,250 --> 00:21:04,770
(Real Madrid Noble,
Spanish National Team Representative)

406
00:21:04,830 --> 00:21:08,330
(Leonardo Luna)
He's very famous in Real Madrid's junior team.

407
00:21:09,289 --> 00:21:12,751
Since you're his brother, you must be
as talented as him.

408
00:21:15,921 --> 00:21:18,980
Blue Lock, third selection.

409
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:20,824
World-class five-on-five selection match.

410
00:21:20,884 --> 00:21:23,020
The rules are the same as the second selection.

411
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,286
The team that scores five points first wins.

412
00:21:24,346 --> 00:21:26,350
We have to win.

413
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:31,061
I'll make them have
a deep impression of me, Yoichi Isagi!

414
00:21:34,182 --> 00:21:35,373
It begins!

415
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:36,310
(Argentina National Team Representative, Freckled Kid)
Famous soccer player,

416
00:21:36,370 --> 00:21:37,174
(Pablo Cavasoz)
Freckled Kid!

417
00:21:37,234 --> 00:21:40,844
This is the debut of the reborn
Meguru Bachira!

418
00:21:40,904 --> 00:21:42,989
What a great spin!

419
00:21:44,410 --> 00:21:45,390
No.

420
00:21:45,450 --> 00:21:47,410
One more touch spin!

421
00:21:48,161 --> 00:21:50,604
Incredible, he passed Cabazos!

422
00:21:50,664 --> 00:21:51,850
Nice, Bachira!

423
00:21:51,910 --> 00:21:52,939
Let's get past him two-on-one!

424
00:21:52,999 --> 00:21:54,560
What nonsense are you saying?

425
00:21:54,620 --> 00:21:58,695
How could I pass the ball
to someone who understands me so well?

426
00:21:58,755 --> 00:22:01,489
Only someone who wants to keep moving forward
can be acknowledged by him.

427
00:22:01,549 --> 00:22:04,111
This is his new playing style.

428
00:22:04,171 --> 00:22:06,536
An incredibly selfish
dribbling style!

429
00:22:06,596 --> 00:22:09,372
Then, I'll adapt myself
to the current you!

430
00:22:09,432 --> 00:22:12,834
I'll work with Bachira
as closely as possible to his prediction.

431
00:22:12,894 --> 00:22:15,086
My target is shooting,
the positioning for that is...

432
00:22:15,146 --> 00:22:16,270
right here!

433
00:22:16,330 --> 00:22:17,357
Bachira, pass the ball!

434
00:22:19,620 --> 00:22:21,092
Where did he come from?

435
00:22:21,152 --> 00:22:24,239
(France Representative, Prodigy, Julian Loki)
Since you've come, I'll crush you!

436
00:22:26,408 --> 00:22:28,159
There it is! The ball is moving fast!

437
00:22:33,290 --> 00:22:35,640
Are you serious? Bachira passed to Rin?

438
00:22:35,700 --> 00:22:37,752
They got inspired by my action

439
00:22:38,211 --> 00:22:40,714
and scored a goal
with a super fast combination play!

440
00:22:43,675 --> 00:22:45,310
Incredible!

441
00:22:45,370 --> 00:22:46,743
Even though the opponents are
world-class selection players!

442
00:22:46,803 --> 00:22:50,307
Producing instant harmony
with unprecedented cooperation.

443
00:22:51,516 --> 00:22:56,169
Right now, they are
showing their greatness to the world.

444
00:22:56,229 --> 00:22:57,837
Not bad.

445
00:22:57,897 --> 00:23:00,108
Seems like they're not amateurs.

446
00:23:04,237 --> 00:23:07,701
Damn, this is interesting.

447
00:23:07,761 --> 00:23:10,290
Next, I have to score a goal!

448
00:23:11,870 --> 00:23:14,938
Blue Lock Extra Scene!

449
00:23:14,998 --> 00:23:16,390
(#23, The Useless Chemical Reaction)
Who threw this carelessly?

450
00:23:16,450 --> 00:23:17,940
(Shouei Barou)
Who threw this carelessly?

451
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,919
It's scattered everywhere!

452
00:23:21,755 --> 00:23:25,390
(Seishiro Nagi)
Why didn't you wake me up?

453
00:23:25,450 --> 00:23:28,928
Eating alone is such a hassle.

454
00:23:30,764 --> 00:23:31,890
(Hyoma Chigiri)
Hey.

455
00:23:31,950 --> 00:23:34,270
Has anyone seen my bandage?

456
00:23:34,330 --> 00:23:36,519
Where did I put it?

457
00:23:38,355 --> 00:23:39,337
Oh, yeah...

458
00:23:39,397 --> 00:23:41,840
(Yoichi Isagi)
Chigiri's care tools are here, right?

459
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:43,049
He always...

460
00:23:43,109 --> 00:23:44,926
Nagi, let's go eat!

461
00:23:44,986 --> 00:23:46,011
That person...

462
00:23:46,071 --> 00:23:48,722
Everyone, is there any more
laundry to wash?

463
00:23:48,782 --> 00:23:51,266
Isagi...

464
00:23:51,326 --> 00:23:54,520
He's the one who left this team
on a whim!

465
00:23:54,580 --> 00:23:57,370
Damn Isagi, I won't forgive you!

466
00:23:57,430 --> 00:23:59,876
So hungry.